{"batchcomplete":"","query":{"pages":{"92019652":{"pageid":92019652,"ns":6,"title":"File:An Experimental Investigation into NOx Control of a Gas Turbine Combustor and Augmentor Tube Incorporating a Catalytic Reduction System (IA anexperimentalin1094543846).pdf","index":7,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":3064706,"width":1275,"height":1650,"pagecount":90,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/An_Experimental_Investigation_into_NOx_Control_of_a_Gas_Turbine_Combustor_and_Augmentor_Tube_Incorporating_a_Catalytic_Reduction_System_%28IA_anexperimentalin1094543846%29.pdf/page1-960px-thumbnail.pdf.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":1600,"thumbheight":2071,"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/An_Experimental_Investigation_into_NOx_Control_of_a_Gas_Turbine_Combustor_and_Augmentor_Tube_Incorporating_a_Catalytic_Reduction_System_%28IA_anexperimentalin1094543846%29.pdf/page1-960px-thumbnail.pdf.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":1600,"height":2071},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/26/An_Experimental_Investigation_into_NOx_Control_of_a_Gas_Turbine_Combustor_and_Augmentor_Tube_Incorporating_a_Catalytic_Reduction_System_%28IA_anexperimentalin1094543846%29.pdf?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:An_Experimental_Investigation_into_NOx_Control_of_a_Gas_Turbine_Combustor_and_Augmentor_Tube_Incorporating_a_Catalytic_Reduction_System_(IA_anexperimentalin1094543846).pdf","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:Redirect/page/92019652","extmetadata":{"Artist":{"value":"<div class=\"fn value\">\nBehrens, Christopher Karl</div>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"ImageDescription":{"value":"<div class=\"description\">\n<p>An initial experimental investigation was conducted to examine the feasibility of NO x emission control using catalytic reduction techniques in the jet engine test cell environment. A modified T-63 gas turbine combustor and an augmentor tube, 21 feet in length and containing a perlite catalyst, were used as a gas generator and catalytic reduction system. Four data runs were made. Three runs were completed without the catalyst installed. Temperature and velocity profile measurements were obtained in order to calculate augmentation ratios for different engine fuel to air ratios.  NOx, CO, and unburned hydrocarbon concentrations in the exhaust were measured to provide a baseline for further tests.  A fourth data run was made with the perlite catalyst installed in the augmentor tube. A 64 percent NOx reduction was observed, however, the large pressure drop across the\ncatalytic bed deemed the current configuration impractical \nRecommendations for alternative configurations are presented.  The results of the investigation have proven that further study is warranted.\n</p>\n<br>Subjects: NOx Control; Gas Turbine Combustors; Emissions Control Exhaust Augmentor Tubes; Gas Analyzers; Pollution Control</div>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""}}}]},"92233977":{"pageid":92233977,"ns":6,"title":"File:An investigation into the effects of vermiculite on NOx reduction and additives on sooting and exhaust infrared signature from a gas turbine combustor (IA aninvestigationi1094537988).pdf","index":16,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":2847985,"width":1275,"height":1650,"pagecount":85,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/An_investigation_into_the_effects_of_vermiculite_on_NOx_reduction_and_additives_on_sooting_and_exhaust_infrared_signature_from_a_gas_turbine_combustor_%28IA_aninvestigationi1094537988%29.pdf/page1-960px-thumbnail.pdf.jpg?utm_source=commo